  "scope": "Symmetric managed TURN, H.264 720p30, NACK/RTX/FlexFEC 5/1, no requested playout-delay hint. Same full stepped-capacity and 120 ms / 30 ms / 2% impairment qualification as the preceding direct/TURN regression. Only generated private encoder configuration differs; production source, pacing and controller code remain unchanged.",
  "interpretation": [
    "The first controller-only trial recovers more quickly, but changes both the loss threshold and hold duration. Its continued-pressure gate fails because a 100% threshold supplies no above-threshold loss observation; the gate is preserved, not reclassified or relaxed.",
    "The two 1% / zero-hold trials do not validate removing the hold. Relay-1 has 13\u201324% reported loss even without injected impairment, remains at the 2 Mbit/s floor and never exercises bitrate recovery. Kernel receive overflow and encoder/host-scheduling gates pass; the loss source remains unresolved.",
    "Relay-2 recovers to 6.8 Mbit/s but fails impairment freezes and scheduling/cadence: host sampler gaps reach 381 ms and one encoded-frame gap reaches 205.530 ms. Host invalidity prevents a stable performance conclusion; it does not excuse the distinct impaired-phase freeze failure.",
    "All four raw results remain failures. The unchanged 1% / 5-second production policy remains pending diagnosis and qualification. No capture-to-display latency claim is made."
